        "description": "Decompose the problem: fix the relative positions of circles (e.g., maintain hexagonal-like structure but allow scaling), and use differential evolution to optimize the absolute radii of all 26 circles simultaneously. The constraint is that circles must not overlap and stay within bounds. Differential evolution (scipy.optimize.differential_evolution) is excellent for global optimization with bounds and can handle the non-convex constraint landscape better than gradient-based methods. For each candidate solution (26 radii values), check validity by computing minimum distances; if valid, return negative sum_radii as fitness. Use bounds [0, 0.15] for each radius. The algorithm will discover which circles should be larger/smaller based on their positions.",
        "what_to_optimize": "individual radii values to exploit position-dependent packing efficiency",
